  "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13972108/assets/0e0941c1d165feb5378d73b69d2fc7bc59a0869e83f78ec064bfb929e1ca21d4.png)\n\nGiven the graph above, solve the inequality $(x+1)(x+6)>0.$",
  "worked_solution": "Notice that our inequality\n\n$$\n(x+1)(x+6)>0,\n$$\n\nis a \"*greater than*\" inequality. Therefore, we need to find the values of $x$ for which the parabola \n\n$$\ny=(x+1)(x+6)\n$$\n\nis *above* the $x$-axis. We mark these values of $x$ in blue in the diagram below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13972108/assets/ae41c9e159852d1b64f3afce5c27ecf7202afd069f33936e7399679edabe4d97.png)\n\nSo, the solution to the inequality is $x<-6$ or $x>-1.$",
